    "body": "## Summary\n- add optional `bio` and `publicLocation` fields to user profiles with Flyway V32 and database invariants\n- extend the authenticated profile update flow so owners can edit/clear both public fields\n- normalize blank optional values to `NULL` server-side\n- enrich `GET /users/{id}/profile` with bio, public location and `memberSince`\n- keep trust signals server-derived: ratings, completed-job counts and verification cannot be edited by clients\n- update the profile settings UI and public profile page with responsive presentation\n- add backend regression coverage for normalization and public profile mapping\n- document profile/privacy semantics in `USER_PROFILES.md`\n\n## Privacy / security\n- `publicLocation` is a free-form label only; it is not geocoded and is not connected to private PostGIS job locations, routes or live tracking\n- public profile responses still exclude email, auth data, wallet/payment data, exact locations, verification documents and moderation data\n- React renders bio as text; the backend does not copy any private job/location field into the profile\n- optional fields are size-limited in validation and constrained against persisted blank values in PostgreSQL\n\n## Validation\nRun Maven verify, frontend dependency audit/lint/build, containers/runtime smoke and applicable payment smoke workflows. Do not merge unless the latest head is fully green.",
